.TH "HTMLMEDIAELEMENT.CURRENTTIME" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLMediaElement.currentTime \- HTMLMediaElement: currentTime property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]HTMLMediaElement\f[R] interface\(cqs
\f[B]\f[CB]currentTime\f[B]\f[R] property specifies the current playback
time in seconds.
.PP
Changing the value of \f[CR]currentTime\f[R] seeks the media to the new
time.
.SH VALUE
A double\-precision floating\-point value indicating the current
playback time in seconds.
.PP
If the media is not yet playing, the value of \f[CR]currentTime\f[R]
indicates the time position within the media at which playback will
begin once the \f[CR]play()\f[R] method is called.
.PP
Setting \f[CR]currentTime\f[R] to a new value seeks the media to the
given time, if the media is available.
.PP
For media without a known duration\(emsuch as media being streamed
live\(emit\(cqs possible that the browser may not be able to obtain
parts of the media that have expired from the media buffer.
Also, media whose timeline doesn\(cqt begin at 0 seconds cannot be
seeked to a time before its timeline\(cqs earliest time.
.PP
The length of the media in seconds can be determined using the
\f[CR]duration\f[R] property.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] video = document.createElement(\(dqvideo\(dq);
console.log(video.currentTime);
.EE
.SH USAGE NOTES
.SS Time precision
The browser does not apply timer rounding to \f[CR]currentTime\f[R],
including values supplied by script.
Seeking can still adjust the resulting playback position to a position
supported by the media.
.PP
The value of \f[CR]currentTime\f[R] is an approximation of the current
playback position.
The browser updates this value as playback progresses.
The \c
.UR https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#official-playback-position
HTML specification
.UE \c
\ requires the reported playback position to remain stable while scripts
are running.
.PP
The update frequency depends on the browser and media playback pipeline.
As a result, successive reads can return the same \f[CR]currentTime\f[R]
even when \f[CR]Date.now()\f[R] has advanced.
The number of decimal places in the value does not indicate how often it
updates or how accurately it matches the audio or video being presented.
.PP
For example, successive readings during playback might produce these
values:
.IP
.EX
video.currentTime;
\f[I]// Might be:\f[R]
\f[I]// 23.404\f[R]
\f[I]// 23.404\f[R]
\f[I]// 23.452\f[R]
\f[I]// \&...\f[R]
.EE
